1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,205
A primitive is a small reusable technical
contribution with a clear contract.

2
00:00:05,275 --> 00:00:09,201
Separate stable behavior from
customer-specific configuration.

3
00:00:09,271 --> 00:00:15,521
Input validation, correlation identifiers, and
idempotent decision recording can generalize

4
00:00:15,591 --> 00:00:19,090
more easily than Northstar’s
exact routing categories.

5
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:23,597
Document inputs, outputs, failure
behavior, tests, and assumptions.

6
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:26,718
Reuse needs a maintainer and a version policy.

7
00:00:26,788 --> 00:00:32,100
A copied file without ownership may multiply
defects rather than reduce future work.

8
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:35,413
The lab routing function
contains category keywords.

9
00:00:35,483 --> 00:00:41,520
Its event-recording contract is more general:
one suggestion identifier can receive only one

10
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:42,827
saved decision.

11
00:00:42,897 --> 00:00:46,865
You can reuse that contract without
adopting the same categories.

12
00:00:46,935 --> 00:00:51,714
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

13
00:00:51,784 --> 00:00:57,288
Extract a primitive proposal with interface,
tests, owner, and local configuration.

14
00:00:57,358 --> 00:00:59,321
Primitive: decision recording.

15
00:00:59,391 --> 00:01:04,020
Input: an existing suggestion
identifier and an allowed chosen queue.

16
00:01:04,090 --> 00:01:06,885
Output: an auditable decision identifier.

17
00:01:06,955 --> 00:01:11,499
Failures: unknown suggestion,
duplicate decision, or invalid queue.

18
00:01:11,569 --> 00:01:13,318
Tests cover each condition.

19
00:01:13,388 --> 00:01:15,628
Queue names remain configuration.

20
00:01:15,698 --> 00:01:20,775
Name a maintainer and record a version
change when contract behavior changes.

21
00:01:20,845 --> 00:01:23,747
Which item is most reusable across domains?

22
00:01:23,817 --> 00:01:25,843
A. Northstar’s sponsor name B.

23
00:01:25,913 --> 00:01:28,196
A fixed access-ticket keyword list C.

24
00:01:28,266 --> 00:01:30,719
A tested decision-recording contract.

25
00:01:30,789 --> 00:01:32,197
The best answer is C.

26
00:01:32,267 --> 00:01:35,574
Stable contracts travel
better than local assumptions.
